community='''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Community · early stage</span><h1 class="page-title">Better questions.<br>Better AI projects.</h1><p>Agent Lab is building a practical place to exchange workflows, lessons, and experiments. Rather than pretend a forum is active before it exists, we're starting with guided discussion topics and an idea-submission channel.</p></div></section><section class="section" style="padding-top:25px"><div class="container"><div class="community-head"><div class="content-panel"><h2>The community we want to build</h2><p>Show what you tried, the problem it solved, what broke, and what you would do differently. Specific experiments beat broad claims.</p><p><strong>Current status:</strong> Discussion boards, profiles, and voting are not live yet. This page contains editorial conversation starters, not user-generated posts.</p><a href="#suggest" class="button primary">Suggest a discussion ↗</a></div><div class="content-panel"><h2>Community principles</h2><ul><li>Share repeatable workflows and honest results.</li><li>Respect privacy, licenses, and platform rules.</li><li>Label affiliations, paid promotions, and affiliate links.</li><li>Ask for evidence before repeating big claims.</li></ul></div></div><div class="section-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Conversation starters</span><h2>Topics worth discussing</h2><p>These are prompts curated by Agent Lab, not community posts.</p></div></div><div class="simple-list"><div class="discussion-card"><small>Workflow critique</small><h3>What is one small AI automation you have actually tested?</h3><p>Include input, steps, costs, failure cases, and time saved if you measured it.</p></div><div class="discussion-card"><small>Build in public</small><h3>Where should a human review stay in the loop?</h3><p>Compare trust, cost, and risk in customer-facing workflows.</p></div><div class="discussion-card"><small>AI for work</small><h3>Which task would you automate first in a tiny service business?</h3><p>Start from an expensive recurring problem, not a favorite tool.</p></div></div><div class="section-spacer"></div><div class="form" id="suggest"><h2>Suggest a discussion topic</h2><p>Send an idea for a future community discussion. Suggestions are private until reviewed and may not be published.</p><form data-inquiry><input type="text" name="website" class="sr-only" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true"><input type="hidden" name="type" value="topic"><div class="field-grid"><div class="field"><label for="t-name">Name *</label><input id="t-name" name="name" required maxlength="120"></div><div class="field"><label for="t-email">Email *</label><input id="t-email" name="email" type="email" required maxlength="254"></div></div><div class="field"><label for="t-message">Your discussion idea *</label><textarea id="t-message" name="message" minlength="20" maxlength="3000" required placeholder="What should people learn or compare?"></textarea></div><p class="form-note">Inquiries work after the site owner configures email delivery.</p><button class="button primary" type="submit">Send inquiry →</button> <button class="button secondary small hidden" type="button" data-copy-inquiry>Copy inquiry</button><div class="form-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></div></form></div></div></section>'''
(ROOT/'community').mkdir(exist_ok=True)
(ROOT/'community/index.html').write_text(layout('Community','Suggest and explore practical AI discussion topics while the Agent Lab community is being built.','Community',community),encoding='utf-8')

about='''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Why Agent Lab exists</span><h1 class="page-title">Less AI noise.<br>More working knowledge.</h1><p>Every day brings new tools, demos, and dramatic promises. Agent Lab focuses instead on the question: what can a person actually build or improve with AI today?</p></div></section><section class="section" style="padding-top:20px"><div class="container"><div class="content-grid"><div class="content-panel"><h2>What we're building</h2><p>A searchable library of practical AI playbooks, with context, implementation steps, documentation references, and caution notes.</p><p>We want to make useful AI more understandable to creators, teams, and small businesses. Agent Lab starts as a curated publication; community discussion, content submissions, and richer tools can follow when we can support them reliably.</p><a class="button primary" href="/directory/">Explore the directory ↗</a></div><div class="content-panel"><h2>What we won't do</h2><ul><li>Promise that using AI will make you a particular amount of money.</li><li>Publish fake case studies or invented community activity.</li><li>Claim a sponsored listing is an independent endorsement.</li><li>Present an editorial estimate as a measured result.</li></ul></div></div><div class="section-spacer"></div><div id="standards" class="content-panel"><span class="eyebrow">How we publish</span><h2>Editorial standards</h2><p><strong>Primary documentation first.</strong> Each initial directory entry links to at least one relevant vendor-maintained resource. These sources support the tools' capabilities, not a guarantee that every proposed workflow will work for every reader.</p><p><strong>Specific and testable.</strong> A useful guide describes the user problem, basic setup, tradeoffs, and an initial verification step. Setup times are editorial estimates and may vary.</p><p><strong>Transparent commercial relationships.</strong> Paid placements and affiliate relationships will be identified near their links or content. Sponsors cannot purchase favorable editorial conclusions.</p><p><strong>Corrections and safety.</strong> Readers should verify facts, protect private information, follow applicable terms, and retain human review for important decisions. Requests for corrections can be sent through our <a class="plain-link" href="/sponsor/#inquiry">contact form</a> once email delivery is configured.</p><p class="disclaimer">Agent Lab is a new project. The editorial library exists; audience metrics, a public forum, and automated content operations are not yet established.</p></div></div></section>'''
(ROOT/'about').mkdir(exist_ok=True)
(ROOT/'about/index.html').write_text(layout('About Agent Lab','Our mission is to make real AI workflows understandable, testable, and responsibly documented.','About',about),encoding='utf-8')

